NAME
    init - VNU userspace init (initialD), PID 1

SYNOPSIS
    /sbin/init

DESCRIPTION
    The first process the kernel starts at boot, and the last one
    standing: it never execs over itself and never exits, so PID 1
    stays valid for the whole boot. Orphans are adopted by it and
    reaped, and the console keeps a login shell because init keeps
    one, respawning it whenever it exits.

    At startup init runs the boot scripts /etc/initialD/*.init in
    lexical order (00-mount.init, 10-services.init), waiting for
    each in turn. A script that fails does not fail the boot: the
    status is reported and the next script runs. Scripts are vash
    scripts and run with the console on stdin/stdout/stderr.

    Afterwards init starts /bin/vash on the console and waits for
    it. Logging out (exit) ends that shell and init starts a fresh
    one, which is why a logout returns to the VNU login: prompt.

    init ignores SIGINT and SIGTERM; to restart the machine use the
    desktop system menu's Reboot item.

FILES
    /etc/initialD/*.init - boot scripts, lexical order
    /tmp/.initialD-boot - trace the boot scripts append to

SEE ALSO
    vash(1), sh(1)
